WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
TLS certificates bind public keys to names for a defined validity period through a

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.885
certificate authority process.

00:00:06.885 --> 00:00:09.910
Certificate transparency logs publish records of many issued certificates,

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.560
helping defenders discover hostnames and monitor unexpected issuance.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.540
A certificate record can support that a certificate covered a name at a point in time.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.550
It does not prove the service is currently online, fully secure,

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.620
owned forever by one organization, or free from compromise.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.680
Wildcards and shared hosting add further ambiguity.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.120
Public web metadata includes response headers, redirects, page titles, linked resources,

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.355
and document metadata.

00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:35.710
These elements may indicate a hosting platform, application framework,

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:39.370
content-management system, provider, or migration path.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.200
Technology fingerprints are probabilistic.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.130
Headers can be removed or changed, products can mimic one another,

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.870
and intermediary services can rewrite responses.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.120
Treat a fingerprint as a lead to validate, not a definitive version inventory.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.120
Redirects and page metadata can connect brands, domains, and services,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.480
but relationships may be temporary or managed by a third party.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.700
Preserve complete redirect context and observation time instead of citing only the final

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.535
destination.

00:01:02.535 --> 00:01:07.595
Use certificate and web metadata defensively to reconcile assets, detect unexpected names,

00:01:07.595 --> 00:01:10.835
review exposure, and prioritize authorized internal validation.

00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:14.340
Do not use public metadata as permission to test authentication,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.380
exploit a suspected product, or retrieve restricted content.
